  data: {
    LLM: 'Each turn: take one card (top of stock or the face-up discard) then discard one card. Only the latest discard may be taken. The first player to lay down three tunnelas or pure sequences chooses a card from the stock as the tiplu (face down under the stock); that rank and the cards immediately above and below it in the same suit become wild (poplu, tiplu, jhiplu). After that, use wild cards to form dirty sets. End by laying all cards in valid sets and discarding one, or by laying eight dublees.',
    Player: 'Each turn: take one card (top of stock or the face-up discard) then discard one card. Only the latest discard may be taken. The first player to lay down three tunnelas or pure sequences chooses a card from the stock as the tiplu (face down under the stock); that rank and the cards immediately above and below it in the same suit become wild (poplu, tiplu, jhiplu). After that, use wild cards to form dirty sets. End by laying all cards in valid sets and discarding one, or by laying eight dublees.',
    objective: 'Be the first to complete three pure sets (tunnelas or pure sequences) to choose or see the tiplu, then arrange all cards into valid three-card sets (and optionally seven or eight dublees) and discard the last card to end the hand. Score the most points from maal and tunnelas.',
    gameplay: 'Each turn: take one card (top of stock or the face-up discard) then discard one card. Only the latest discard may be taken. The first player to lay down three tunnelas or pure sequences chooses a card from the stock as the tiplu (face down under the stock); that rank and the cards immediately above and below it in the same suit become wild (poplu, tiplu, jhiplu). After that, use wild cards to form dirty sets. End by laying all cards in valid sets and discarding one, or by laying eight dublees.',
    keyRules: [
      '21 cards each; draw one, discard one each turn',
      'Only the top card of the discard pile may be taken',
      'First to lay three pure sets chooses the tiplu',
      'Valid sets: tunnela (3 identical), pure sequence (3 consecutive same suit), trial (3 same rank different suits), dirty versions with wilds',
      'Eight dublees (pairs of identical cards) can also win; jokers cannot form dublees',
